=== PARITY (web Popover.tsx reproduced — contract, composition, states, i18n) ===
  The web component is a lightweight positioning primitive (no data hooks, anonymous,
  no charts/maps). Apple's system popover provides the SAME contract natively and is
  the house idiom (LayoutSwitcher / SettingField / AlertMessageEditor all use
  `.popover` + `.presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)`). Mapping:
    web prop / behavior            → native mechanism
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    anchorRef                      → the modified (trigger) view (`.tsPopover` on it)
    open / onClose                 → isPresented binding + onDismiss on open→closed
    side = 'bottom'|'top'          → arrowEdge + attachmentUnitPoint.y  (PopoverPlacement)
    align = 'start'|'center'|'end' → attachmentUnitPoint.x ∈ {0, 0.5, 1}
    sideOffset = 6                 → padding on the content's anchor-facing edge
    auto-flip on overflow          → system popover flip (PopoverSide.flipped documents it)
    viewport clamp (margin 8)      → system popover safe-area clamp (PopoverMetrics.margin)
    Esc / outside-pointer dismiss  → native popover dismissal (+ onDismiss)
    restore focus to trigger       → system restores focus to the presenting control
    aria-modal="false" (non-trap)  → NO `.isModal` trait (children stay reachable)
    role="dialog" + aria-label     → .accessibilityElement(.contain) + .accessibilityLabel
    children                       → the @ViewBuilder content the caller hands it
    surface (rounded/border/shadow/--surface-1/--text-primary)
                                   → system popover chrome + .presentationBackground(
                                     Color.TS.surface) + Color.TS.textPrimary
  No web Tailwind ported; platform tokens (P1/S9: Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing /
  TSRadius) used throughout.

=== STATES (every branch the web source carries is reproduced) ===
  The web Popover owns NO data lifecycle — it positions whatever children it is
  handed — so loading/empty/error/stale/offline belong to the content a caller hosts
  inside the popover, NOT to the primitive (identical precedent: the merged pure
  presentational sibling KioskOverlay 0124, documented in its log/header). The render
  branches the web source DOES carry are reproduced + tested:
    closed (`!open` → null)        → not presented (binding false → nothing rendered)
    open + positioned              → system-positioned per PopoverPlacement
    flipped (overflow)             → system flip (PopoverSide.flipped, tested)
    clamped (viewport edge)        → system safe-area clamp
  (The web pre-measurement `visibility:hidden @ -9999` branch is a DOM-measurement
  artifact the system popover has no analogue for — it measures atomically.)

